            "Assuming that rows without an onset are not validated"
        ],
        "explanation": "A row whose onset is n/a is not merged with any other row, but its assembled annotation (the HED column joined with the annotations of its sidecar-annotated columns) is still validated like any other row's. A tag that appears both in the HED column and in the sidecar annotation of the same row is repeated at the top level, wherever the row sits in the file.",
        "correction_strategy": "Remove the tag from the HED column or from the sidecar annotation",
        "correction_examples": [
            {
                "wrong": "event_code show -> \"Sensory-event, Visual-presentation\" with HED column \"Sensory-event, Red\"",
